# Trivy ignore file for infra/terraform (wired into .github/workflows/infra-validate.yaml).
#
# These stacks provision throwaway, public, cheap GPU *test* clusters (see
# infra/AGENTS.md) — not production. Entries here should be misconfigs that are
# intentionally N/A for that context (e.g. production-hardening policies that
# don't apply to ephemeral test infra, or would add cost/scope the design
# deliberately rejects). Fix a finding instead of ignoring it when it's cheap
# and sensible — this file is a curated baseline, not a blanket suppression.
#
# Left empty for now: the first CI run against `aquasec/trivy:0.58.1 config`
# reveals what, if anything, needs suppressing at HIGH/CRITICAL severity.
# Add entries as `AVD-...` / `CKV_..._...` IDs with a one-line reason once real
# findings are triaged — do not pre-guess check IDs here.
